From a599028101974d6724846567840248741a7d6482 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:42:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Discord alerts: link a game account with ::discord, and
 trading post news arrives as a DM

A bot in its own worker thread (server/discord/DiscordThread.ts, discord.js 14) sends
every trading post notice - an offer on your listing, your offer accepted, declined, or
beaten to it, your item bought - to the player's Discord as a DM, whether they are
online or not. It is off unless DISCORD_TOKEN and DISCORD_GUILD_ID are set in .env.

LINKING PROVES BOTH ENDS. ::discord in game gets a six-character code (no 0/O or 1/I/L -
it is read off the game screen); /link <code> in the server's Discord links the Discord
account that typed it to the game account that asked. A code is good once, for ten
minutes. /unlink or ::discord unlink undoes it; /linked lists what is linked. The three
slash commands are registered as guild commands when the bot starts, so they appear at
once rather than after global propagation.

A WORKER, because discord.js keeps a gateway socket with its own heartbeat and a DM is
an HTTP round trip that can be slow or rate-limited, and none of that belongs on the
tick. The world posts {type: 'notify'} and never waits; the worker owns the bot and its
link table (data/discord/<profile>.sqlite, apart from everything else). The trading
post reaches it through the notice hook TradingPost.ts has carried since it was
written.

If the bot is not in the server DISCORD_GUILD_ID names, startup says so and prints the
bot's own invite link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
